## Planned audio-engine dependencies

These are not shipped yet. They are listed here so the license position is
reviewed before the engine work lands.

| Component | Used for | License |
| --- | --- | --- |
| cpal | Native audio output in the Rust engine | Apache-2.0 OR MIT |
| symphonia | Decoding MP3, AAC/M4A, FLAC, Ogg/Vorbis, Opus, WAV | MPL-2.0 |

MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: modifications to Symphonia's own files must be
published under MPL-2.0, while OpenDeck's files can remain MIT. We do not
modify Symphonia; if that changes, the modified files will be called out here.

## Development and verification tools

`node:test`, the TypeScript compiler, Cargo and the browser/CDP tooling used in
the verification notes are development-only and are not redistributed with the
application.

## Reference material

The Serato file-format behaviour implemented by the import/export code was
documented from publicly available community reverse-engineering notes
([serato-tags](https://github.com/Holzhaus/serato-tags), the Mixxx wiki and
[rb2serato](https://github.com/SM4RTENHEIMER/rb2serato), all MIT-licensed
documentation/projects). No source code from those projects is vendored into
OpenDeck; see `docs/interop.md` for the specific claims and links.
